Feature: SQL Aggregation of Sales Data by Brand, Product, Market, Competitor Flag, Channel, and Transaction Time

  This feature specifies the technical requirements for aggregating sales data from the purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly table. The aggregation must be performed for each unique combination of brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name, and transaction_timestamp, with conditional logic and strict validation rules.

  Background:
    Given the source table is purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly
    And the columns to aggregate are integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars
    And the aggregation keys are brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name, transaction_timestamp
    And only rows where market_normalized_name is "trastuzumab-anns", "bevacizumab-awwb", or "rituximab market" are included
    And only rows where transaction_timestamp is within the last 36 months from cdl_effective_date are included
    And for rows where brand_normalized_name is "kanjinti", "mvasi", or "riabni" and br_gpo_flag contains "KAISER" (case-insensitive), integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are treated as zero before aggregation

  Scenario: Aggregate sales data for valid rows (happy path)
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name "kanjinti"
    And normalized_name "Herceptin"
    And market_normalized_name "trastuzumab-anns"
    And competitor_flag false
    And channel_name "Hospital"
    And transaction_timestamp "2023-05-15T00:00:00"
    And integrated_units 100
    And integrated_normalized_units 95
    And integrated_dollars 12000.50
    And br_gpo_flag "ABC GPO"
    And cdl_effective_date "2023-06-01"
    When the SQL script is executed
    Then the row is included in the aggregation
    And the aggregated integrated_units is 100
    And the aggregated integrated_normalized_units is 95
    And the aggregated integrated_dollars is 12000.50

  Scenario: Exclude rows with invalid market_normalized_name
    Given a row with market_normalized_name "other-market"
    When the SQL script is executed
    Then the row is excluded from the aggregation

  Scenario: Exclude rows with transaction_timestamp outside 36 months window
    Given a row with transaction_timestamp "2019-01-01T00:00:00"
    And cdl_effective_date "2023-06-01"
    When the SQL script is executed
    Then the row is excluded from the aggregation

  Scenario Outline: Set sales values to zero for specific brands and GPO flag containing "KAISER"
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name <brand>
    And normalized_name <product>
    And market_normalized_name <market>
    And competitor_flag <competitor>
    And channel_name <channel>
    And transaction_timestamp <timestamp>
    And integrated_units <units>
    And integrated_normalized_units <normalized_units>
    And integrated_dollars <dollars>
    And br_gpo_flag <gpo_flag>
    And cdl_effective_date <cdl_date>
    When the SQL script is executed
    Then the aggregated integrated_units is 0
    And the aggregated integrated_normalized_units is 0
    And the aggregated integrated_dollars is 0

    Examples:
      | brand     | product    | market             | competitor | channel   | timestamp           | units | normalized_units | dollars   | gpo_flag         | cdl_date    |
      | kanjinti  | Herceptin  | trastuzumab-anns   | false      | Hospital  | 2023-05-15T00:00:00 | 100   | 95              | 12000.50  | KAISER PERMANENTE| 2023-06-01  |
      | mvasi     | Avastin    | bevacizumab-awwb   | true       | Clinic    | 2022-11-10T00:00:00 | 50    | 48              | 8000.00   | Kaiser Northwest | 2022-12-01  |
      | riabni    | Rituxan    | rituximab market   | false      | Pharmacy  | 2021-07-20T00:00:00 | 30    | 29              | 5000.00   | kaiser south     | 2021-08-01  |

  Scenario Outline: Do not set sales values to zero for specific brands if GPO flag does not contain "KAISER"
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name <brand>
    And normalized_name <product>
    And market_normalized_name <market>
    And competitor_flag <competitor>
    And channel_name <channel>
    And transaction_timestamp <timestamp>
    And integrated_units <units>
    And integrated_normalized_units <normalized_units>
    And integrated_dollars <dollars>
    And br_gpo_flag <gpo_flag>
    And cdl_effective_date <cdl_date>
    When the SQL script is executed
    Then the aggregated integrated_units is <units>
    And the aggregated integrated_normalized_units is <normalized_units>
    And the aggregated integrated_dollars is <dollars>

    Examples:
      | brand     | product    | market             | competitor | channel   | timestamp           | units | normalized_units | dollars   | gpo_flag         | cdl_date    |
      | kanjinti  | Herceptin  | trastuzumab-anns   | false      | Hospital  | 2023-05-15T00:00:00 | 100   | 95              | 12000.50  | ABC GPO          | 2023-06-01  |
      | mvasi     | Avastin    | bevacizumab-awwb   | true       | Clinic    | 2022-11-10T00:00:00 | 50    | 48              | 8000.00   | XYZ GPO          | 2022-12-01  |
      | riabni    | Rituxan    | rituximab market   | false      | Pharmacy  | 2021-07-20T00:00:00 | 30    | 29              | 5000.00   | Some GPO         | 2021-08-01  |

  Scenario Outline: Exclude rows with NULL or invalid cdl_effective_date
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name <brand>
    And normalized_name <product>
    And market_normalized_name <market>
    And competitor_flag <competitor>
    And channel_name <channel>
    And transaction_timestamp <timestamp>
    And integrated_units <units>
    And integrated_normalized_units <normalized_units>
    And integrated_dollars <dollars>
    And br_gpo_flag <gpo_flag>
    And cdl_effective_date <cdl_date>
    When the SQL script is executed
    Then the row is excluded from the aggregation
    And an error message "Invalid cdl_effective_date" is logged

    Examples:
      | brand     | product    | market             | competitor | channel   | timestamp           | units | normalized_units | dollars   | gpo_flag         | cdl_date    |
      | kanjinti  | Herceptin  | trastuzumab-anns   | false      | Hospital  | 2023-05-15T00:00:00 | 100   | 95              | 12000.50  | KAISER PERMANENTE| NULL        |
      | mvasi     | Avastin    | bevacizumab-awwb   | true       | Clinic    | 2022-11-10T00:00:00 | 50    | 48              | 8000.00   | Kaiser Northwest | INVALID     |

  Scenario Outline: Aggregate multiple rows for the same combination
    Given multiple rows with the same brand_normalized_name <brand>, normalized_name <product>, market_normalized_name <market>, competitor_flag <competitor>, channel_name <channel>, and transaction_timestamp <timestamp>
    And the rows have integrated_units <units1> and <units2>
    And the rows have integrated_normalized_units <normalized_units1> and <normalized_units2>
    And the rows have integrated_dollars <dollars1> and <dollars2>
    And br_gpo_flag <gpo_flag1> and <gpo_flag2>
    And cdl_effective_date <cdl_date>
    When the SQL script is executed
    Then the aggregated integrated_units is <units1> + <units2>
    And the aggregated integrated_normalized_units is <normalized_units1> + <normalized_units2>
    And the aggregated integrated_dollars is <dollars1> + <dollars2>

    Examples:
      | brand     | product    | market             | competitor | channel   | timestamp           | units1 | units2 | normalized_units1 | normalized_units2 | dollars1 | dollars2 | gpo_flag1 | gpo_flag2 | cdl_date    |
      | kanjinti  | Herceptin  | trastuzumab-anns   | false      | Hospital  | 2023-05-15T00:00:00 | 100    | 50     | 95                | 45                | 12000.50 | 6000.00  | ABC GPO   | ABC GPO   | 2023-06-01  |
      | mvasi     | Avastin    | bevacizumab-awwb   | true       | Clinic    | 2022-11-10T00:00:00 | 50     | 30     | 48                | 28                | 8000.00  | 4000.00  | XYZ GPO   | XYZ GPO   | 2022-12-01  |

  Scenario: Case-insensitive matching for GPO flag "KAISER"
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name "kanjinti"
    And br_gpo_flag "kaiser permanente"
    When the SQL script is executed
    Then integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are set to zero before aggregation

  Scenario: Aggregation with competitor_flag true and false
    Given two rows with identical brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, channel_name, transaction_timestamp
    And one row has competitor_flag true, the other false
    When the SQL script is executed
    Then the aggregation is performed separately for each competitor_flag value

  Scenario: Data type validation for aggregation columns
    Given a row with integrated_units as integer
    And integrated_normalized_units as integer
    And integrated_dollars as double
    When the SQL script is executed
    Then the aggregation is performed without type errors

  Scenario: Exclude rows with NULL in aggregation keys
    Given a row with NULL in brand_normalized_name
    Or NULL in normalized_name
    Or NULL in market_normalized_name
    Or NULL in competitor_flag
    Or NULL in channel_name
    Or NULL in transaction_timestamp
    When the SQL script is executed
    Then the row is excluded from the aggregation
    And an error message "Missing aggregation key" is logged

  Scenario: Error handling for invalid transaction_timestamp format
    Given a row with transaction_timestamp "invalid-timestamp"
    When the SQL script is executed
    Then the row is excluded from the aggregation
    And an error message "Invalid transaction_timestamp format" is logged
